# Documentation moved to its own site, built from the horsie repo.
# Rules match top-down, so the two old page URLs come before the catch-all and
# the catch-all comes before the SPA fallback.
#
# The old site had exactly two doc pages and its paths share no shape with the
# new ones, so a path-preserving splat here would 301 every old link to a 404 —
# which it did. Map the two that existed, and send anything else to the docs
# home rather than to a URL invented from the old path.
/docs/introduction   https://docs.horsie.dev/start-here/what-horsie-is/          301
/docs/architecture   https://docs.horsie.dev/internals/sessions-and-durability/  301
/docs                https://docs.horsie.dev/                                    301
/docs/*              https://docs.horsie.dev/                                    301

# BrowserRouter needs every other path served the app shell.
/*                   /index.html                                                 200
